{
  "_readme": "Curated Instagram feed for the site (4 Oct 2026; refreshed weekly from 13 Oct). 'mock': true marks a post whose cover shows pre-production renders; the card carries a Mock-up label. One object per post. 'id' is the Instagram shortcode; the post date is decoded from it at build time (Instagram media ids carry their timestamp), so there is no date field to keep in sync. 'label' is OUR wording for the site, never a copy of the caption (some older captions predate the brand rules). 'src' is the folder in Social Media/ that holds the slides, for covers and the on-site step-through; a post with no src gets its cover from uploads/ig/<id>.webp only. Covers: uploads/ig/<id>.webp (1080x1350) and <id>-540.webp. Slides: uploads/ig/s/<id>/NN.mp4. A post whose cover file is missing is skipped by the build, so the site never shows an empty card. The home strip opens on the newest post (no pin since 17 Oct 2026). To add a post: add an object at the top, drop its cover (and slides) in, rebuild.",
